      "message": "Also, can you see what these cmake checks are looking for exactly?\n\n```\n-- Performing Test STD_REGEX -- failed\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/host_command_common.o\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/hwtimer32.o\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/spi.o\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/spi_controller-stm32h7.o\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/system.o\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/trng.o\n-- Performing Test GNU_POSIX_REGEX -- failed\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/uart.o\n  CC      RW/chip/stm32/watchdog.o\n  CC      RW/common/console.o\n  CC      RW/common/console_output.o\n  CC      RW/common/debug.o\n-- Performing Test POSIX_REGEX -- failed\n\u001b[31mCMake Error at third_party/benchmark/CMakeLists.txt:325 (message):\n  Failed to determine the source files for the regular expression backend\n```\n\nAs mentioned, I don\u0027t think we explicitly disabled `std::regex`, so I would expect the `STD_REGEX` check to pass.",
