      "writtenOn": "2026-06-18T00:07:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "BoringSSL binds benchmarks to BUILD_TESTING unconditionally, so they cannot be disabled separately. Disabling  BUILD_TESTING  unblocks the GCC/glibc upgrade now without patching BoringSSL. We can address FPMCU tests separately later if needed.\n\nI compiled std_regex.cpp in the chroot using the FPMCU cross-compiler, armv7m-cros-eabi-clang++. It failed at the link stage with:\nld.lld: error: unable to find library -lgcc_eh\nSeems the bare-metal toolchain does not include/support exception handling runtimes, so test fails.",
      "parentUuid": "7a4974f5_6b81f288",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "285d2053df3f692876992cd7194b18a251abc8c5",
